          "text": "Supportless, free-form 3D printing! ⛓️\n\nBy using low-melting-point Fields' metal and shaping it through surface tension, this process can create highly conductive 3D structures in a single pass, no supports, no post-processing. \n\nPretty interesting way of thinking about additive manufacturing, especially for electronics and functional metal parts.\n\nJust wow. I only know this is from Singapore, anyone has more information about them?\n\n~~ \n\n♻️ Join the weekly robotics newsletter, and never miss any news → https://t.co/GoA3ZuwoPB"
